It is early evening in the park, but the sun is still high in the sky.
Jonas and Nele are sitting with me on the grass.
Jonas has already started the grill.
He has brought sausages and vegetables for everyone.
We eat the Brötchen and enjoy the warmth.
Nele looks at the sky.
"It is almost eight o'clock, and it is still so bright!" she says.
I nod and am really amazed by the late light.
I tell Jonas and Nele about my family in Mexico.
"Last year I had a massive barbecue party at home," I say.
"We celebrated all day in the garden."
"Was the food different with your family?" Jonas asks.
"Oh yes, the food was of course much spicier!" I answer laughing.
"We had so many different sauces on the table."
"But we did not have this long summer light in the evenings."
We continue to relax on the warm grass.
I love these late, bright summer evenings in Berlin.
